  "summary": {
    "key_finding": "Unconstrained Full TTA forces 100% abstention/freezing due to negative true utility under severe camera-trap shifts, replicating the CCT-20 safe-utility-only result. In contrast, Entropy-Gated Partial TTA and Head-Only TTA restrict drift amplification, enabling KGA to soundly certify positive adaptation on moderate-shift locations with zero false-adaptations.",
    "remedy_proposal": "For natural non-i.i.d. deployment shifts, future certified adaptation should constrain candidate updates to prediction heads or entropy-gated normalization layers, transforming purely conservative retention into opportunistic safe adaptation."
  }
